    <section class="section" id="doc-overview" aria-labelledby="doc-overview-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 &middot; Overview</p>
        <h2 id="doc-overview-title">Overview <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <p><strong>BinaryRevisionWithProtocol is an open protocol for immutable file revisions, transactional multi-file changes, diff, restore, and crash-safe workspace projection — without requiring Git.</strong></p>
        <p>A Revision is one immutable state of one logical file. A RevisionSet groups revisions across one or more files into a reviewable logical transaction. FileHead points at the currently accepted revision. Workspace Projection materializes accepted state as ordinary files.</p>
        <p>Git is not required and not replaced. Implementations can run standalone or coexist with Git or other source-control systems. <a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-architecture" aria-labelledby="doc-architecture-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 &middot; Architecture</p>
        <h2 id="doc-architecture-title">Architecture <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">component flow</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>Physical File
     |
     `-- .vsn Sidecar
             |
             v
         Revision
             |
             v
       RevisionSet
             |
             v
          FileHead
             |
             v
   Workspace Projection</code></pre></div>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="mono">Revision</td><td>Immutable state of one file.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">RevisionSet</td><td>Logical transaction / change set.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">ApplyTransaction</td><td>Physical projection and recovery transaction.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">FileHead</td><td>Canonical accepted state pointer.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Workspace files</td><td>Materialized projection of accepted state.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">DiffArtifact</td><td>Derived, disposable comparison.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    <section class="section" id="doc-vsn" aria-labelledby="doc-vsn-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 &middot; .vsn Sidecar</p>
        <h2 id="doc-vsn-title">.vsn Sidecar <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <p><strong>.vsn is a companion sidecar file that travels with its logical file and carries its revision state/history and the information required to reconstruct or locate those revisions.</strong></p>
        <p>Normative terms in this page follow RFC 2119: MUST / MUST NOT are absolute requirements, SHOULD / SHOULD NOT are strong recommendations with documented exceptions, and MAY marks truly optional behavior.</p>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">file-local sidecars</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>project/
`-- src/
    |-- Program.cs
    |-- Program.cs.vsn
    |-- UserService.cs
    `-- UserService.cs.vsn</code></pre></div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>One logical file maps to one sidecar: <code class="inline-code">Program.cs</code> + <code class="inline-code">Program.cs.vsn</code>.</li>
          <li>The sidecar carries FileId, revision history, revision metadata, accepted/head information, revision references, and references to content/revision data.</li>
          <li>A valid sidecar MUST embed every byte required to reconstruct each retained Revision. External storage MAY exist for sync, cache, backup, or collaboration, but it MUST NOT be required for retained-revision reconstruction.</li>
          <li><code class="inline-code">FileId</code> is authoritative identity. Filename is not identity.</li>
          <li>Rename preserves FileId; move preserves FileId.</li>
          <li>The <code class="inline-code">.vsn</code> file is not the protocol itself. It is one representation/storage mechanism for the protocol; other backends can exist.</li>
          <li>Design goal: copy both files to another workspace and the revision history travels with them.</li>
        </ul>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Intended behavior</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Rename file</td><td>Same FileId, sidecar follows the logical file.</td><td>Specification</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Move file</td><td>Same FileId, sidecar follows the logical file.</td><td>Specification</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Copy both files</td><td>History travels with the pair.</td><td>Specification</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sidecar missing</td><td>Behavior not yet frozen; do not assume recovery.</td><td>Planned</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sidecar corrupted</td><td>Behavior not yet frozen; do not assume recovery.</td><td>Planned</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Physical file deleted</td><td>Behavior not yet frozen.</td><td>Planned</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-revision" aria-labelledby="doc-revision-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 &middot; Revision Model</p>
        <h2 id="doc-revision-title">Revision Model <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">immutability</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>Revision A
    |
    v
Revision B
    |
    v
Revision C</code></pre></div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>A Revision is one immutable state of one logical file.</li>
          <li>A committed Revision is never rewritten.</li>
          <li>Revisions remain addressable according to retention policy; old revisions may be purged only under documented GC rules.</li>
          <li>Restore creates new revision state based on an old revision; it never mutates the source revision.</li>
          <li>Workspace files are projections; FileHead represents accepted state.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    <section class="section" id="doc-identity" aria-labelledby="doc-identity-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 &middot; File Identity</p>
        <h2 id="doc-identity-title">File Identity <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <p><strong>FileId is the authoritative identity of a logical file.</strong> Identity is not inferred from path, filename, content hash, size, timestamp, similarity, or delete/create proximity.</p>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">rename preserves identity</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>src/A.cs
    |
    v rename
src/B.cs
    FileId unchanged</code></pre></div>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">move preserves identity</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>src/A.cs
    |
    v move
tests/A.cs
    FileId unchanged</code></pre></div>
        <p>Deleting one file and creating another with identical bytes does not automatically make them the same logical file.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-revisionset" aria-labelledby="doc-revisionset-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 &middot; RevisionSet</p>
        <h2 id="doc-revisionset-title">RevisionSet <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">public lifecycle</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>DRAFT
  |
  v
PENDING_REVIEW
  |
  v
ACCEPTING
  |
  v
ACCEPTED

PENDING_REVIEW --&gt; REJECTED
ACCEPTING -----&gt; CONFLICTED
DRAFT ---------&gt; ABORTED</code></pre></div>
        <p><code class="inline-code">SEALED</code> is not a public RevisionSet state. <code class="inline-code">RECOVERY_REQUIRED</code> is not a RevisionSet state; recovery belongs to ApplyTransaction. Sealing is an operation, not a state.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-content" aria-labelledby="doc-content-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">07 &middot; Content Model</p>
        <h2 id="doc-content-title">Content Model <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">references</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>Revision
   |
   `-- ContentRef
          |
          `-- Content Object / Storage</code></pre></div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>ContentRef identifies raw logical bytes by SHA-256 and exact byte size.</li>
          <li>Canonical form: <code class="inline-code">sha256:&lt;64 lowercase hexadecimal characters&gt;</code>.</li>
          <li>Hash is computed over raw file bytes before compression, encryption, or storage transformations.</li>
          <li>Binary-safe: arbitrary bytes are first-class. No newline or encoding normalization.</li>
          <li>LF and CRLF remain distinct byte sequences; BOM remains content; invalid UTF-8 is not silently replaced.</li>
          <li>ContentRef is authoritative for identity; DiffArtifact is derived.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    <section class="section" id="doc-diff" aria-labelledby="doc-diff-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">08 &middot; Diff</p>
        <h2 id="doc-diff-title">Diff <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">derived comparison</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>Revision A
    |
    +-- Compare --+
    |             |
    v             v
Revision B --&gt; DiffArtifact</code></pre></div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>DiffArtifact is derived, reproducible, and disposable. It is never canonical revision state.</li>
          <li>Restore does not depend on DiffArtifact for reconstructing the source revision.</li>
          <li>Exact diff modes are not frozen in this repository yet; document them only when implemented.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-restore" aria-labelledby="doc-restore-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">09 &middot; Restore</p>
        <h2 id="doc-restore-title">Restore <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Intended scopes: <code class="inline-code">CONTENT_ONLY</code>, <code class="inline-code">CONTENT_AND_PATH</code>, <code class="inline-code">FULL_STATE</code>.</li>
          <li>Restore points at a source revision and creates new state; it never rewrites the source.</li>
          <li>Restore reconstructs from revision content, not from DiffArtifact.</li>
          <li>Scope/source matrix, ABSENT behavior, and failure rules are not frozen yet; no implementation found in this repository.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-apply" aria-labelledby="doc-apply-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">10 &middot; ApplyTransaction</p>
        <h2 id="doc-apply-title">ApplyTransaction <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <p><strong>RevisionSet is the logical change transaction. ApplyTransaction is the physical workspace projection and recovery transaction.</strong></p>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">intended states</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>PREPARING -&gt; PREPARED -&gt; PROJECTION_APPLYING -&gt; PROJECTION_APPLIED
  -&gt; LOGICAL_COMMITTING -&gt; LOGICALLY_COMMITTED -&gt; FINALIZED
ROLLING_BACK -&gt; ROLLED_BACK
* -&gt; RECOVERY_REQUIRED (physical recovery only)</code></pre></div>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-recovery" aria-labelledby="doc-recovery-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">11 &middot; Crash Recovery</p>
        <h2 id="doc-recovery-title">Crash Recovery <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">commit marker rule</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>LogicalCommitMarker absent
    -&gt; accepted state remains old
    -&gt; rollback projection

LogicalCommitMarker present
    -&gt; accepted state is new
    -&gt; roll forward projection
    -&gt; finalize</code></pre></div>
        <p><code class="inline-code">RECOVERY_REQUIRED</code> is a physical ApplyTransaction recovery state, not a RevisionSet state. It is not evidence that a RevisionSet was accepted or rejected.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-commit" aria-labelledby="doc-commit-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">12 &middot; Logical Commit</p>
        <h2 id="doc-commit-title">Logical Commit <span class="spec-tag">Specification</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">acceptance invariant</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>RevisionSet = ACCEPTED
        &lt;=&gt;
Logical Commit exists</code></pre></div>
        <p>Logical commit updates canonical accepted state (FileHeads, path index, WorkspaceVersion, LogicalCommitMarker, accept idempotency result). Physical projection finalization is separate cleanup.</p>
        <p>Conflict path: <code class="inline-code">ACCEPTING -&gt; conflict -&gt; CONFLICTED</code>. No logical commit, FileHeads unchanged, partial projection rolled back.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-rcmp" aria-labelledby="doc-rcmp-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">13 &middot; Serialization / RCMP-1</p>
        <h2 id="doc-rcmp-title">Serialization / RCMP-1 <span class="spec-tag">Planned</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">intended pipeline</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>Semantic Record
      |
      v
RCMP-1 Canonical Bytes
      |
      v
Deterministic bytes
      |
      v
SHA-256</code></pre></div>
        <p>No RCMP-1 encoder, schema, or byte-level test vector was found in this repository. The intended rules (MessagePack arrays, deterministic ordering, UUID/hash/timestamp/UTF-8 encoding, no floating point in core records, extension maps with numeric keys) remain planned. No hexadecimal examples are included because none exist in the implementation.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    <section class="section" id="doc-digest" aria-labelledby="doc-digest-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">14 &middot; MembersDigest</p>
        <h2 id="doc-digest-title">MembersDigest <span class="spec-tag">Planned</span></h2>
        <div class="code-card"><div class="code-head"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="code-title mono">intended algorithm</span></div>
<pre class="mono tree"><code>Members
  |
  v sort by Ordinal
Require contiguous ordinals
  |
  v canonical RCMP-1 array
SHA-256 -&gt; sha256:&lt;64 lowercase hex&gt;</code></pre></div>
        <p>No implementation or test vector found; do not treat this as verified behavior yet.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-idempotency" aria-labelledby="doc-idempotency-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">15 &middot; Idempotency</p>
        <h2 id="doc-idempotency-title">Idempotency <span class="spec-tag">Planned</span></h2>
        <p>Intended key: <code class="inline-code">RevisionSetId + StageOperationId</code>. Retry, concurrent retry, reservation, request digest, result reuse, and orphaned-content handling are not verified against code in this repository.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-gc" aria-labelledby="doc-gc-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">16 &middot; Garbage Collection</p>
        <h2 id="doc-gc-title">Garbage Collection <span class="spec-tag">Planned</span></h2>
        <p><strong>Invariant:</strong> every retained or addressable Revision must remain fully reconstructable byte-for-byte.</p>
        <p>No GC implementation, roots, leases, holds, grace periods, or purge ordering were found in this repository. Revision metadata reachability vs. content reachability is specified but not verified.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="doc-security" aria-labelledby="doc-security-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">17 &middot; Security</p>
        <h2 id="doc-security-title">Security <span class="spec-tag">Planned</span></h2>
        <p>No path/filesystem enforcement code was found in this repository. Intended rules (workspace-relative paths, absolute-path and <code class="inline-code">..</code> rejection, NUL rejection, symlink/junction handling, TOCTOU protection) remain specification only.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
      </div>
    <section class="section" id="doc-conformance" aria-labelledby="doc-conformance-title">
      <div class="container doc">
        <p class="eyebrow">18 &middot; Conformance</p>
